.TH HDPASSW 1 "2026-05-24" "hdpassw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hdpassw \- deterministic password manager backed by a BIP39 seed phrase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hdpassw
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hdpassw
derives passwords deterministically from a single BIP39 seed phrase.
No passwords are ever stored.
Every password is computed on demand from the seed phrase, the site name,
the username, and a rotation counter.
.PP
Back up 24 words offline and recover every password, forever.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "hdpassw seed new"
Generate a new random 24-word BIP39 mnemonic and print it.
Write it down and store it offline before using it.
.SS "hdpassw seed check"
Interactively validate a mnemonic phrase without deriving any keys.
.SS "hdpassw gen \fISITE\fR"
Derive the password for \fISITE\fR and copy it to the clipboard.
The clipboard is automatically cleared after 30 seconds (see \fB\-\-clip-timeout\fR).
If \fISITE\fR exists in the metadata file its settings are used automatically;
otherwise \fB\-\-user\fR is required.
.PP
.RS
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
Username or email address for this site.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-counter\fR \fIN\fR
Rotation counter (default: from metadata, or 1).
Increment to rotate the password for this site without affecting others.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-length\fR \fIN\fR
Password length in characters (default: from metadata, or 32).
.TP
\fB\-\-charset\fR \fINAME\fR
Character set to use.
Valid values: \fBalpha\fR, \fBalphanumeric\fR (default), \fBfull\fR, \fBpin\fR, \fBhex\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-reveal\fR
Print the password to stdout instead of copying to the clipboard.
Use only in a trusted terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-clip-timeout\fR \fISECS\fR
Seconds before the clipboard is cleared (default: 30).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output metadata as JSON (password is not included unless \fB\-\-reveal\fR is also set).
.RE
.SS "hdpassw add \fISITE\fR"
Add or update the metadata record for \fISITE\fR.
No password material is stored — only site name, username, counter,
length, charset, and a 4-character non-secret verifier.
.SS "hdpassw ls [\fIFILTER\fR]"
List all known sites, optionally filtered by a substring.
Pass \fB\-\-json\fR for machine-readable output.
.SS "hdpassw rm \fISITE\fR"
Remove the metadata record for \fISITE\fR.
Prompts for confirmation unless \fB\-y\fR is given.
.SS "hdpassw export"
Print the full metadata file to stdout in TOML format.
Contains no passwords or key material.
.SS "hdpassw recover \fISITE\fR"
Scan counters 1..N until the derived verifier matches \fB\-\-verifier\fR.
Useful when the metadata file is lost but the verifier was noted separately.
.PP
.RS
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
Username to use during the scan.
.TP
\fB\-\-verifier\fR \fIHEX\fR
4-character hex verifier to match (from the metadata file or your notes).
.TP
\fB\-\-max-counter\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum counter value to try (default: 20).
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
These flags are accepted by every command.
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fIFILE\fR
Path to the metadata file (default: \fI~/.config/hdpassw/sites.toml\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\fR \fIPHRASE\fR
BIP39 passphrase (second factor).
Prefer the environment variable \fBHDPASSW_PASSPHRASE\fR over this flag to
avoid the passphrase appearing in the process argument list.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help for the current command.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBHDPASSW_PASSPHRASE\fR
BIP39 passphrase. Equivalent to \fB\-\-passphrase\fR but safer for scripting.
.TP
\fBHDPASSW_MNEMONIC\fR
Seed phrase. Intended for CI/testing only.
A warning is printed whenever this variable is set.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/hdpassw/sites.toml\fR
Metadata file. Contains site names, usernames, counters, and non-secret
verifiers. No passwords or key material. Safe to back up anywhere.
Permissions are set to 0600 (owner read/write only) on Unix.
.SH CHARSETS
.TP
\fBalphanumeric\fR
a\-z A\-Z 0\-9 (62 characters, default)
.TP
\fBalpha\fR
a\-z A\-Z (52 characters)
.TP
\fBfull\fR
a\-z A\-Z 0\-9 and common symbols (95 printable ASCII characters)
.TP
\fBpin\fR
0\-9 (10 characters, for numeric PINs)
.TP
\fBhex\fR
0\-9 a\-f (16 characters, for API keys and hex secrets)
.SH BACKUP STRATEGY
.TP
\fBSeed phrase (24 words)\fR
Secret. Store offline on paper or a metal backup.
This is the only thing that must be kept secure.
.TP
\fBPassphrase\fR
Secret. Memorise it; never write it next to the seed phrase.
.TP
\fB~/.config/hdpassw/sites.toml\fR
Not secret. Store in git, cloud storage, or anywhere convenient.
Losing it is recoverable: all passwords at counter=1 need only the seed phrase;
rotated passwords can be found with \fBhdpassw recover\fR if the verifier is known.
.SH CRYPTOGRAPHY
Password derivation follows a three-step pipeline:
.PP
.RS
seed phrase → PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 (BIP39) → 64-byte seed
.br
seed[0:32]  → HKDF-Extract SHA-256 ("hdpassw-v1") → master key
.br
master key  → HKDF-Expand SHA-256 (site|user|counter) → site key
.br
site key    → HKDF-Expand SHA-256 ("encode") → password
.RE
.PP
See \fIALGORITHM.md\fR in the source tree for the full specification including
test vectors.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a new seed phrase:
.PP
.RS
.EX
hdpassw seed new
.EE
.RE
.PP
Register a site and generate its password:
.PP
.RS
.EX
hdpassw add github.com --user jakob
hdpassw gen github.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Rotate the password for one site (all others unchanged):
.PP
.RS
.EX
hdpassw add github.com --user jakob --counter 2
hdpassw gen github.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Recover the correct counter from seed alone:
.PP
.RS
.EX
hdpassw recover github.com --user jakob --verifier a3f9
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR age (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1),
.BR gpg (1)
